package Patterns;

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Q19 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Please enter n: ");
        int n = input.nextInt();
        for (int i = 1; i <=n ; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <=n-i; j++) {
                System.out.print("*");

            }

            for (int j = 0; j <2 * (i-1); j++) {
                    System.out.print(" ");
                }
            for (int x = 0; x <=n-i; x++) {
                System.out.print("*");

            }

            System.out.println();
        }

        for (int i = 2; i <=n ; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <=i; j++) {
                System.out.print("*");

            }
            for (int j = 0; j <2 * (n- i); j++) {
                System.out.print(" ");
            }
            for (int j = 1; j <=i; j++) {
                System.out.print("*");

            }
            System.out.println();
        }

Approach

The pattern is divided into two symmetric halves:

Upper Half

For each row i from 1 to n:

Print (n - i + 1) stars on the left side.
Print 2 × (i - 1) spaces in the center.
Print (n - i + 1) stars on the right side.

As we move downward:

Stars decrease by 1 on both sides.
Spaces increase by 2.

Example (n = 5):

**********
****  ****
***    ***
**      **
*        *
Lower Half

For each row i from 2 to n:

Print i stars on the left side.
Print 2 × (n - i) spaces in the center.
Print i stars on the right side.

As we move downward:

Stars increase by 1 on both sides.
Spaces decrease by 2.

Example:

**      **
***    ***
****  ****
**********
Key Observation
The pattern remains symmetric about the vertical center.
The number of stars and spaces change in opposite directions.
Upper half:
Stars ↓
Spaces ↑
Lower half:
Stars ↑
Spaces ↓
Formulas
Upper Half:
Left Stars  = n - i + 1
Spaces      = 2 × (i - 1)
Right Stars = n - i + 1

Lower Half:
Left Stars  = i
Spaces      = 2 × (n - i)
Right Stars = i
Time Complexity

There are 2n - 1 rows.

Each row prints approximately 2n characters (stars + spaces).

Time Complexity: O(n²)
Space Complexity

No extra data structure is used apart from loop variables.

Space Complexity: O(1)
